-- title:
--   Equal doubled residues have exactly three possible integer representative relations
-- statement:
--   Equal doubled residues have exactly three possible integer representative relations.
--
--   Let $n>0$ and write $I_n=\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z$, represented by $0,\ldots,n-1$. The symbol $\operatorname{rep}$ takes a residue to its nonnegative representative and leaves ordinary integers unchanged. Residue sums and differences are cyclic; inequalities use representatives. $\mathfrak S(I_n)$ is the permutation group. Function symbols are written in curried notation; a subscript $\#$ means finite cardinality.
--
--   The precise quantified assertion, with all its hypotheses, is
--
--   $$
--   \forall  (n : \mathbb N_{>0}) (i j : I_{n}), i + i = j + j \to  2\, \operatorname{rep}\,i = 2\, \operatorname{rep}\,j \lor  2\, \operatorname{rep}\,i + n = 2\, \operatorname{rep}\,j \lor  2\, \operatorname{rep}\,j + n = 2\, \operatorname{rep}\,i
--   $$
--
--   This result is used to constrain the remaining phases or to construct a sorting word with the stated cost.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/snow-ghost/glushkov-lx-lean/blob/8cddcd222b591673dc63475d9d45b9ed5c6eb92c/LX/ReflectionPhases.lean#L51-L65

